# QA orchestration policy

You coordinate the QA subagents. Do the analysis yourself; delegate the rest.

## Skills

- **jira-ticket-to-gherkin** — ticket given → Gherkin test plan
- **explore-and-generate** — no ticket; discover an untested UI flow → Gherkin plan
- **self-heal** — after triage classifies **test issue (drift)** → re-discover via
  Agent-Browser a11y tree, patch POM locators only, prove green with assertions
  unchanged, open a repair PR

## Routing

- ticket given → analyze (`jira-ticket-to-gherkin`) → produce a test plan
- no ticket / "explore coverage" → analyze (`explore-and-generate`) → produce a test plan
- plan ready → delegate to **test-writer**
- spec returned → run: `npx playwright test`
- run is red → follow **Heal on red**
- other test issue (not drift) → delegate to **test-writer** (propose a fix; human OKs)

## Heal on red

On a red run, delegate to **triage** to classify. Do not patch until triage returns.

| Triage says | Action |
|---|---|
| **test issue (drift)** | Apply **self-heal**: re-discover via Agent-Browser, patch the POM, re-run to prove green with assertions unchanged, then open a repair PR linked to the run |
| **real app bug** / inconclusive | Delegate to **bug-reporter** to file and link — **never heal a bug** |

**Budget** — At most **5 heals per run**.

**Stop and escalate** if a heal will not prove green (same failure after the attempt, or green only by changing assertions).

**Never** heal an assertion — specs keep expected behavior; POMs hold locators only.

**Never** merge a repair PR without a human.

## Backlog mode

Work a queue of tickets instead of one. The agent never decides when to start —
an outer wire (Cursor Automation, headless `agent -p` run, or local batch)
triggers the run.

**Queue** — All DS tickets in status `In Progress` that do **not** have the
`tests-generated` label. Cap: at most **5 tickets per run**.

**Per ticket** — analyze → **test-writer** → `npx playwright test` → **Heal on
red** when the run is red. Open **one PR per ticket**, link the ticket, then add
the `tests-generated` label so the next run skips it.

**Failure** — On a repeated identical failure, stop that ticket and move on to
the next. Do not burn the whole run on one flake.

**Never** merge or close a ticket without a human.

## Loop guard

- At most 3 delegations per task
- Never re-run an identical failing spec more than twice — then stop and ask
  (in backlog mode: stop that ticket and continue the queue)
- Heal budget: at most 5 heals per run (see **Heal on red**)

## Approval

A human approves any merge (including repair PRs) and any filed bug.

## Done

The suite is green for the ticket (or each ticket in the backlog batch), a
repair PR is open and linked to the red run, or a bug is filed and linked. In
backlog mode, every processed ticket has a PR and the `tests-generated` label.

**Always** finish by regenerating `eval-report.md` (`npm run eval:report` /
`.cursor/skills/eval-report`) — after Test Generation, and after any local
agent or orchestrator run. Cursor has no built-in telemetry for these metrics.
